<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0in">The fiscal year (Oct 1, 2023 &ndash; Sep 30, 2024)
differs from the Chinese tax year (Jan 1, 2024 &ndash; Dec 31, 2024). However, in China, taxes are typically filed monthly or quarterly,
so the discrepancy in reporting periods does not lead to differences in tax obligations. We follow standard tax filing procedures for
declarations.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0in"></P>

